tortoise-wow: VMaNGOS Eluna methods and the Lua instance AI survive a gone
object, and a map state that is not available on the calling thread.

Aura:GetCasterLevel called aura->GetCaster()->GetLevel(). GetCaster is a guid
lookup (SpellAuras.cpp) that returns null once the caster despawned or logged
out, which a DoT whose caster died leaves behind; a player caster is also looked
up on every map. It returned nil's level through a null pointer (SIGSEGV). It
now pushes nil when the caster is gone, and also when the caster is on another
map than the state's (this core refuses objects of another map in a map state,
0002), and keeps pushing the level otherwise.

Item:GetItemLink read item->GetOwner()->GetLevel(). An item without an owner
(dropped, in a chest, in the mail) has none; the link's level field is 0 then.

ElunaInstanceAI's hooks and data methods called instance->GetEluna()->... with
no check. Map::GetEluna returns the map's state only to the thread that updates
the map (core, this PR), so it can be null where the instance AI still runs:
a missing state is now treated as "no script", as ElunaCreatureAI does since
0007. Update, IsEncounterInProgress, OnPlayerEnter, OnObjectCreate,
OnCreatureCreate, Initialize, Load, Save, GetData, SetData, GetData64 and
SetData64 check the state. Load copies its data into lastSaveData before that
check, so data that arrives while the state is missing is kept and reloaded on
the map's next update (Reload); it used to return before the copy and lose it.
Save returns NULL and does not touch lastSaveData: InstanceData::SaveToDB
(src/game/Maps/InstanceData.cpp) skips the write when Save returns NULL, so the
stored data stays; the one caller that stores an empty column for NULL,
DungeonPersistentState::SaveToDB (MapPersistentStateMgr.cpp), runs for a new
instance only (AddPersistentState with !load), where empty data is correct.
Returning lastSaveData there would read it off that thread while the map
thread rewrites it. The data getters return 0.

Upstreamable: ALE has the same GetCasterLevel (mod-ale methods/AuraMethods.h),
and the instance AI checks are harmless on cores whose Map always has a state.

Base: ElunaLuaEngine/Eluna 1b06f28ff3a00054d915d824c725fb4283fee74d (branch
cmangos-spell-update), the dep/Eluna pin, with patches 0001-0009 applied. Eluna is
GPL-3.0 (https://github.com/ElunaLuaEngine/Eluna, LICENSE); this change is under
the same licence. Applied by cmake/ElunaSources.cmake to a copy in the build tree.
